Be assured that I not only looked at the code but let it run with code
that output the result of the inner part of rn2(...) code. I even had
one time a gnome with a magic missile generated. Not often but it does
happen.

How do you calculate that it this snippet always yields 0?

difficulty is "int difficulty = monstr[(monsndx(pm))];" the monster
difficulty. The player's experience level doesn't even enter the
equation here. It only does before that regarding what monsters have
been generated before. But I don't think we disagree that gnomes are
generated in the mines.

So, a gnome has 3 as monster difficulty:

rn2(9 - (3 < 4) + 4 * (3 > 6))
rn2(9 - 1 + 4 * 0))
rn2(8)

This will give you a value from 0 to 7 which means a wand of striking
or a wand of magic missile are possible.

If it returns 0 it doesn't yield a helmet either. The code checks if
the monster is *wearing* a helmet and if it does it returns a scroll
of earth. Otherwise it falls through the wand of striking.

